                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7f237c6d-e414-331b-9605-edbf119fa0d7",
                        "entry_id": "349f55ee-c762-3543-a852-0c6485167ce5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An error; a mistake."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "75e25b1c-d9b6-4cae-9089-ba727346e872",
                                "sense_id": "7f237c6d-e414-331b-9605-edbf119fa0d7",
                                "text": "Instant replays highlighted the glaring error, but none of the five officials on the pitch were actually allowed to use video evidence to see what a ricket they'd made of it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab45c9f8-b415-4556-84f7-79cbafa67585",
                                "sense_id": "7f237c6d-e414-331b-9605-edbf119fa0d7",
                                "text": "Superintendent Butler said that after he had been questioned at Cannon Row police station Wilson said, \"You obviously know a lot. I've made a ricket somewhere. I'll have to take my chance. I don't see how you can make it stick without the poppy—and you won't find that.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15ac52ea-4649-4ffe-bed7-165441b23ab2",
                                "sense_id": "7f237c6d-e414-331b-9605-edbf119fa0d7",
                                "text": "You could get really neurotic if you listened to everything that people say about you when you concede a goal. I know when I've had a bad game, when I have dropped a ricket."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
